  "notes": "Composed of {脱|だつ} (to remove, to take off) + {衣|い} (clothing). Most commonly encountered in compound words like {脱衣所|だついじょ} (changing room) and {脱衣|だつい}かご (undressing basket), especially at public baths, hot springs, and swimming pools.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {脱衣所|だついじょ}: changing room; undressing room\n- {脱衣|だつい}かご: basket for clothes (at a bathhouse)\n- {脱衣|だつい}する: to undress\n- {脱衣場|だついば}: changing area\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {着替|きが}え: changing clothes — implies putting on different clothes, not just removing them\n- {更衣|こうい}: changing clothes — a more formal synonym, as in {更衣室|こういしつ} (changing room)",
